# {{projectName}}

A minimal-but-functional **ticketing system** built on the
[Frappe Framework](https://frappeframework.com){{#if withHelpdesk}} and
[Frappe Helpdesk](https://github.com/frappe/helpdesk){{/if}}, scaffolded by
[`dude`](https://github.com/cubocicloide/dude) (stack: `frappe`).

Beyond running out of the box, this project is a **worked example of Frappe's
core building blocks**: the custom app in [`apps/ticketing/`](apps/ticketing/)
demonstrates DocTypes (models), controllers, form scripts and portal pages
(views), whitelisted API methods, scheduled tasks, document-event hooks,
workflows and fixtures — so you can copy the patterns into your own apps.

## Quickstart

```bash
# One-time: the global launcher + project toolchain
npm install -g @cubocicloide/dude-launcher
pnpm install

# Start everything (first boot provisions the bench + site: several minutes)
dude up
dude logs --service bench   # watch the provisioning progress
```

When `bench start` is up:

| What | Where |
| ---- | ----- |
| Desk (admin UI) | http://{{projectName}}.localhost:8000/app — `Administrator` / `admin` |
{{#if withHelpdesk}}| Helpdesk (agent UI) | http://{{projectName}}.localhost:8000/helpdesk |
{{/if}}| Example portal page | http://{{projectName}}.localhost:8000/ticket_stats |
| Example API method | http://{{projectName}}.localhost:8000/api/method/ticketing.api.ticket_stats |

> `*.localhost` resolves to 127.0.0.1 in modern browsers. If your tooling
> can't resolve it, add `127.0.0.1 {{projectName}}.localhost` to `/etc/hosts`.

## Everyday commands

```bash
dude up [--build]        # start the stack
dude down [--volumes]    # stop it (--volumes wipes bench + database!)
dude logs [--service s]  # follow logs
dude shell [--service s] # shell into a container (default: bench)
dude bench <anything>    # raw bench passthrough, e.g. `dude bench --site all migrate`
dude site migrate        # bench migrate on the default site
dude site console        # IPython with the site loaded
dude site backup         # backup database + files
dude app new --name x    # scaffold a new custom app into apps/
dude test                # run the ticketing app's tests
dude lint                # Frappe best-practice structural checks
dude format              # ruff format + autofix over apps/
dude docs                # serve the project docs (MkDocs)
```

Run `dude help` for the full, live catalog{{#if withIac}} — including the
`dude iac …` group that deploys this project to AWS ECS Fargate (see
`iac/README.md`){{/if}}.

## Learn Frappe with this repo

Start with [`apps/ticketing/README.md`](apps/ticketing/README.md) — it maps
each Frappe concept to a concrete file. The project docs (`dude docs`) include
a guided tour and a "how do I add a new DocType / task / workflow?" cookbook.

The structural conventions the linter enforces are described in
[`.claude/rules/`](.claude/rules/) — useful reading even if you never open
the linter.
